//Member Functions or Member Methods
A member function is a function declared inside a class.

Example:

class Student {
public:
    string name;
    int age;

    void study() {
        cout << "Student is studying";
    }
};

Here study() is a member function because it is inside the Student class.

An object can call it using the dot (.) operator:

Student s1;
s1.study();
Simple definition

A member function is a function inside a class that defines what an object can do.

For example:

Student → class
name, age → data members
study() → member function
s1 → object

